      "evidence": "**Evidence:**\n- The Census Bureau's FT-900 archive remains publicly accessible back to **1992** (full historical releases at census.gov/foreign-trade/Press-Release/ft900_index.html), with the joint goods-and-services series complete from January 1994.\n- Bulk historical data tables (nominal and real, seasonally adjusted and not) remain available back to **1985/1987** by classification system.\n- The Census International Trade API (2010\u2013present), USA Trade Online, and historical tools remain operational.\n- No reports of any FT-900 release, exhibit, or historical table being removed or altered. (Archived releases are intentionally frozen vintages, which is a documented feature, not a removal.)\n- No known data elements have been dropped from current releases relative to prior cycles; the December 2025 release announced a forthcoming change to Exhibit 14 (a routine methodological exhibit change), not a removal.\n\n**Risk level: No Known Issue.** The historical record is intact, deep, and accessible through multiple channels.\n\n---"
