      "evidence": "**Evidence for \"Gone\":** None found. No reporting of wholesale removal of prior-year USAspending data.\n\n**Evidence for \"High Risk\":** None found. Award archives (FY2008\u2013present) and account data (FY2017 Q2\u2013present) remain downloadable; a December 2025 GitHub issue shows users successfully pulling full FY2025 files (`FY2025_070_Assistance_Full_20251206.zip`).\n\n**Evidence for \"Moderate Risk\":** No data elements are known to have been removed from historical records. Adjacent feeder-system events are worth noting but do not alter USAspending's historical files: anonymous FPDS access was temporarily disabled in January 2025 (then restored) \u2014 an access change at a *source* system, not a deletion of USAspending history.\n\n**Evidence for \"No Known Issue\":** Historical data remain accessible via the Download Center, API, and full database snapshot with no known alterations. The high-profile 2025 data removals (e.g., DOGE's \"wall of receipts\" stripping USAID contract details, per CBS News) occurred on **doge.gov**, not USAspending.gov \u2014 USAspending was in fact used by NPR and Bloomberg to *fact-check* those removals.\n\n**Assessment: No Known Issue.** Historical files remain intact and downloadable. (Caveat: the dataset has no formal versioning, so silent corrections are always possible \u2014 an inherent design trait, not a 2025 development.)\n\n---"
